B8 pre-delivery checks, 2026-11-13/14 (runs 20:40 UTC 13 Nov - 18:52 UTC 14 Nov)
Tools: Verilator 5.020 2024-01-01 rev (Debian 5.020-1); Tcl 8.6; LibreOffice (workbook recalculation)
Every run below goes through the delivered scripts: regress.tcl and sweep.tcl run unchanged under tclsh with
stand-ins for xvlog, xelab and xsim that build the same testbench with the same defines in Verilator and run it
with the same plusargs (a Verilator build per testbench and define set, like xsim's work folders). The VCS and
Xcelium scripts ran the same way with stand-ins for vcs and xrun. Nothing below ran on xsim, VCS or Xcelium.

== 0. Merge
B8's testbench work (begun before B7 closed) was merged onto the final B7 files: tests_perf, stats, perf_probe,
tests_stress (new), mesh_bench, mesh_top, sched_ref, ctrl_checker, tests_ctrl, tb_mesh_d. B7's last fixes
(tb_demand_counter, tb_sched_ctrl, tb_ctrl_chain, the README, the bundle, xsim_lib's TRACE support) kept.

== 1. Portability scans (README Section 2, rules 1, 9 and 10) on the B8 files
Rule 9: no cast of a call, field, array element or negation inside an expression in the lines B8 adds.
Two loops without a fixed bound in tasks (time passes in every iteration): tests_stress.svh:64 (S01's segments,
each waits wait_cycles) and tests_perf.svh:216 (the TRACE loop, @(posedge clk) each turn). Every other finding
is in lines unchanged since B2-B7. No keywords as names, no empty string parameters, no translate_off outside
the pragma form. Rule 1: no random draw on the right of && in tests_stress (one draw per statement).
A comment line that begins with the word Verilator is read by Verilator as a directive (/*verilator ...*/):
one such line in tests_stress.svh broke the first build and was reworded (Verilator only; xsim ignores it).

== 2. RTL lint (verilator --lint-only -Wall): mesh_top with its new clamp parameters
mesh_top defaults; design D 8x8; K_LO=0; K_HI=7; K_HI=31; REGION_N=2 with K_HI=19; 4x4/2 with K_HI=3: clean,
except K_LO=0 (E7's ablation only): UNSIGNED on sched_ctrl.sv:99, `kt < kl_t'(K_LO)` is constant with K_LO=0,
so the lower clamp does nothing, as intended. Not changed: sched_ctrl is a closed B7 file and its default
configuration is clean. The 16x16 design-D mesh does not fit Verilator on this machine (as in B6 and B7).

== 3. The controller's clamp through mesh_top (K_LO, K_HI; E7 and E8), CT04 and CT05 on 4x4
K_HI = 7 (-define TB_K_MAX=7): CT04 PASS checks=3048318 errors=0; CT05 PASS checks=1058053 errors=0: k_L reaches 7 and
the bound holds at 7. A mutant of mesh_top that gives sched_ctrl D18's K_MAX (15) instead of K_HI: CT04
FAIL checks=3062875 errors=28 (the checker's plans stop at 7, the controller's at 15).
K_LO = 0 (-define TB_K_MIN=0): CT04 failed at the end of c), 'k_L 1 after 6 epochs of traffic across regions,
expected K_MIN 0'. Not the clamp: the controller checker agreed with every plan. On 4x4 with 2x2 regions a packet
spends its last hops in its destination's region, so traffic only across regions still makes share bin 7 (local
demand 7/16 to 8/16 of the total), whose table entry is 1 (0 needs a bin of 3 or less). CT04 c) took K_MIN from the
mesh's clamp in B8 and expected it exactly; it now expects the table's entry for the last epoch's bin, which must
be at most max(K_MIN, 1): the same check as before with D18's K_MIN of 1 (one TB_CHECK, so every count stays).
After the change:
  CT04           CT04   tb_mesh_d              PASS    checks=3,062,877 errors=0 (expected 3,062,877), 34,863 cycles, 247 s
  kmin0 CT04: RESULT CT04 PASS checks=3062877 errors=0 seed=1
  CT04 c) across regions: plans 4 2 1 1 1 1; share bin of the last epoch 7, the table's entry 1
  kmax7 CT04: RESULT CT04 PASS checks=3048318 errors=0 seed=1
  CT04 c) across regions: plans 2 1 1 1 1 1; share bin of the last epoch 7, the table's entry 1
  CT04_8         CT04   tb_mesh_d              PASS    checks=20,335,604 errors=0 (expected 20,335,604), 77,901 cycles, 509 s
  8x8 (CT04_8): CT04 c) across regions: plans 1 1 1 1 1 1; share bin of the last epoch 7, the table's entry 1
On 8x8 too, traffic only across regions makes bin 7, whose entry there is also 1 (0 needs a bin of 4 or less).
A mutant that gives sched_ctrl D18's K_MIN instead of K_LO is not caught on 4x4: with K_LO = 0 it failed the old
CT04 c) exactly as the delivered sources did (FAIL checks=3062877 errors=1), since the tests' lowest local share on 4x4
(CT04 c)) makes bin 7, where K_LO = 0 and 1 give the same plans. On 8x8 see E7's K_MIN 0 points in section 8.

