  Uniform: the plans are E1_8x8_D's with K_MIN 1 (4 2 1 1 1 1): on 8x8 uniform traffic makes share bins whose
  table entry is 1 (bins 5-8; 0 needs a bin of 4 or less), so K_MIN 0 is not reached below saturation and E7's
  K_MIN 0 points would repeat D_PROP's. Hotspot: k_L reached 0 in the last epoch only, with the mesh past
  saturation (accepted 0.0673 of 0.1271 flits/node/cycle offered, sat = 1, mean latency 91,580 cycles: the
  source queues held the backlog of five epochs of warm-up, so the run took 345,509 cycles instead of 173,909).
  Hotspot's RATE_FRAC is a share of uniform saturation (sat_rate() depends only on N and V), but one node that
  receives 20 % of all packets saturates far earlier: its ejection port takes 1 flit per cycle, so on 8x8
  (0.2 x 63 + 0.8) x 2.32 flits x rate <= 1 gives rate <= 0.032 packets/node/cycle, 0.24 of sat_rate()'s 0.137
  (4x4: 0.11, about 0.44 of 0.257). E1's hotspot points from 0.3 (8x8) or 0.5 (4x4), E7's from 0.4 and all 12 of
  E9's (0.5 and 0.9) are past saturation. Not changed here: the experiment plan is yours (see the delivery message).

