== 10. Chart workbook (results/templates/sweep_charts.xlsx)
Built from the example sweep (4x4, designs A-D and design D's SQRT and no-damping variants, uniform and
transpose at 0.1-1.0 of saturation, and one phase-traffic point with +TRACE=1024); recalculated in LibreOffice:
42,703 formulas, no error value; Excel 2007 functions only (no MINIFS or MAXIFS). Charts checked as rendered.
What the example shows: under transpose design A (XY) saturates at 0.6 of saturation while B-D (adaptive)
carry 1.0; under uniform traffic the bypass carries 0.1-0.5 % of packets on 4x4; under phase traffic design D's
k_L goes 2 -> 9 -> 12 -> 14 -> 15 within four epochs when the traffic turns region-local and back to 2.

== 11. After your xsim runs of 14 Nov (R-1114-01 to 10)
Passed as here: quick 22 of 22, S01-S03 short and S02, S03 full, s04 16 of 16, S06 (16 SAME, 'S06 PASS'), CT04.
Two failures, both in B8's tests, not in the RTL, and both out of Verilator's sight:
- S05 failed on every design from cycle 6 (R-1114-02, 04), with Verilator's check counts. It checked whole records
  for X; but like buffer storage the data fields of output registers have no reset and hold X until first written,
  and a port at the mesh's edge never writes them. Verilator is two-state and has no X, so it could not see this.
  S05 now checks every valid bit and every field of a record whose valid bit is 1 (still five checks per tile and
  cycle, so every count stays).
- S01 in full stopped on every design at 6,000,000 cycles (R-1114-07 to 10): the bench's safety net fails a run
  still going after 5,000,000 cycles plus N08's length, and S01 runs 10,000,000. Verilator ran S01 for 2,000,000
  only. The net now adds S01's length (10,000,000 or +S01_CYCLES) when +TEST=S01: a stand-alone check of the new
  initial block gives 16,000,000 cycles for S01, 8,000,000 with +S01_CYCLES=2000000, 6,000,000 for every other test.
