Design A and design B with XY routing (deadlock-free) level off at 0.32. Minimal adaptive routing on every VC lets
cycles of waiting packets form once the mesh saturates, and only the bypass timetable breaks them (D06, BP08), when
the waiting pair's turn comes: in design B about every 800 cycles on 4x4 and 10,500 on 8x8 (C and D across regions
1,250-1,480 and 13,000-22,000). On 4x4 no design collapses. Design D collapses at 0.97 of B's knee and, five epochs
of warm-up behind it, fails to drain past it: its 8x8 sweep points stop at 0.95 of the knee (D61). Tracker: Issues.
